1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,190
Almost four hundred years ago,

2
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:07,290
a scientist called Jan van Helmont
planted a small willow tree in a pot of

3
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:08,520
dried soil.

4
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:10,380
He weighed the tree.

5
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:12,240
He weighed the soil.

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,080
Then, for five years,

7
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,640
he gave it nothing but
water. The tree grew.

8
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:22,910
It gained about seventy-four
kilograms. And the soil?

9
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:26,140
It had lost only about
fifty-seven grams.

10
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:32,800
So where did a whole tree's worth
of mass come from? Not the soil.

11
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,110
Most of the wood came
out of thin air.

12
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:38,540
By the end of this video,

13
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:40,290
you'll know exactly how,

14
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:43,260
and how to explain it in an exam.

15
00:00:46,610 --> 00:00:50,180
You eat to get your
food. Plants don't.

16
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:52,220
Plants make their own food,

17
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:53,900
by photosynthesis.

18
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:57,580
Here's the definition
the mark scheme wants.

19
00:00:57,580 --> 00:00:59,980
Learn it word for word.

20
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:04,340
Photosynthesis is the process by
which plants synthesise carbohydrates

21
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,720
from raw materials
using energy from light.

22
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:10,530
Let's break that down.

23
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:12,400
Synthesise means make.

24
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:15,030
The carbohydrate it makes is glucose,

25
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:16,550
a simple sugar.

26
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:20,120
The raw materials are
carbon dioxide and water.

27
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:23,580
And the energy to do
it comes from light.

28
00:01:24,530 --> 00:01:26,490
Now the word equation.

29
00:01:26,490 --> 00:01:28,630
Carbon dioxide, plus water,

30
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:31,130
gives glucose, plus oxygen.

31
00:01:31,430 --> 00:01:35,370
And it happens in the presence
of light and chlorophyll,

32
00:01:35,370 --> 00:01:38,050
so we write those on the arrow.

33
00:01:38,050 --> 00:01:40,750
They're conditions, not reactants.

34
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:42,500
Light isn't a substance,

35
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:45,000
and chlorophyll isn't used up.

36
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,720
So where do the raw
materials come from?

37
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:52,580
Carbon dioxide diffuses
into the leaf from the air.

38
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:55,880
Water is absorbed from
the soil by the roots,

39
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:57,770
and travels up the stem,

40
00:01:57,770 --> 00:02:00,400
in the xylem, to the leaf.

41
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,950
Oxygen is a waste product.

42
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:06,060
Some is used in the
plant's own respiration,

43
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:10,440
and the rest diffuses out
of the leaf, into the air.

44
00:02:11,390 --> 00:02:13,920
If you're taking the Extended paper,

45
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:17,500
you also need the
balanced symbol equation.

46
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:20,840
Six C O two, plus six H two O,

47
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:23,510
gives C six H twelve O six,

48
00:02:23,510 --> 00:02:25,370
plus six O two.

49
00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:27,880
Let's check it balances.

50
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:30,040
Carbon: six on the left,

51
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,750
six on the right.

52
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:34,470
Hydrogen: twelve on each side.

53
00:02:34,470 --> 00:02:38,340
Oxygen: twelve plus six
makes eighteen on the left,

54
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:43,430
and six plus twelve makes eighteen
on the right. It balances.

55
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:47,600
So, what does the light actually do?

56
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:51,320
Inside the cells of a
leaf are chloroplasts.

57
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:53,480
Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll,

58
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,350
a green pigment.

59
00:02:55,350 --> 00:02:57,420
Chlorophyll absorbs light.

60
00:02:57,420 --> 00:03:01,610
Then it transfers energy from
light into energy in chemicals,

61
00:03:01,610 --> 00:03:04,310
for the synthesis of carbohydrates.

62
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:08,700
In other words, that energy
ends up stored in glucose.

63
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:11,940
Be careful with your wording here.

64
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:15,080
Never write that
chlorophyll makes energy.

65
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:16,940
Energy can't be made.

66
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:18,960
Chlorophyll transfers it.

67
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:22,170
So use the syllabus word: transfers.

68
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:25,660
So the plant has made glucose.

69
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:27,470
What happens to it?

70
00:03:27,470 --> 00:03:30,060
There are five uses to learn.

71
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:33,390
One. Glucose is used in respiration,

72
00:03:33,390 --> 00:03:36,470
to release energy for
the plant's cells.

73
00:03:36,470 --> 00:03:39,450
Two. Glucose is turned into starch,

74
00:03:39,450 --> 00:03:41,260
as an energy store.

75
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,770
Starch is insoluble,

76
00:03:42,770 --> 00:03:47,310
so storing it doesn't affect the
movement of water by osmosis.

77
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:50,680
Three. Glucose is used
to make cellulose,

78
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:53,030
which builds the cell walls.

79
00:03:53,030 --> 00:03:57,540
Four. Glucose is changed
into sucrose, another sugar.

80
00:03:57,540 --> 00:04:00,170
Sucrose is transported in the phloem,

81
00:04:00,170 --> 00:04:03,740
to other parts of
the plant. And five.

82
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:06,070
Sugars are used to make nectar,

83
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:09,840
in flowers, to attract
insects for pollination.

84
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:12,470
Respiration. Starch.

85
00:04:12,470 --> 00:04:15,590
Cellulose. Sucrose. Nectar.

86
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:18,880
But glucose only contains carbon,

87
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,650
hydrogen and oxygen.

88
00:04:20,650 --> 00:04:23,560
To grow, a plant also needs proteins,

89
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:26,640
and proteins are made
from amino acids.

90
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:29,250
Amino acids contain nitrogen.

91
00:04:29,250 --> 00:04:32,410
So plants absorb nitrate
ions from the soil,

92
00:04:32,410 --> 00:04:34,180
through their roots.

93
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:37,600
Nitrate ions are needed
to make amino acids.

94
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:39,260
Without enough nitrate,

95
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:41,400
the plant has stunted growth,

96
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:44,190
and its older leaves turn yellow.

97
00:04:44,690 --> 00:04:47,340
Plants also absorb magnesium ions.

98
00:04:47,340 --> 00:04:50,770
Magnesium ions are needed
to make chlorophyll.

99
00:04:50,770 --> 00:04:52,530
Without enough magnesium,

100
00:04:52,530 --> 00:04:55,710
the leaves turn yellow
between the veins.

101
00:04:55,710 --> 00:04:58,880
Less chlorophyll means
less light is absorbed,

102
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:01,340
so there's less photosynthesis.

103
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:04,390
In an exam, link three things:

104
00:05:04,390 --> 00:05:07,000
the ion, what it's used to make,

105
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,450
and what happens without it.

106
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:13,280
Most photosynthesis
happens in the leaves,

107
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:16,120
and leaves are adapted for it.

108
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,710
Most leaves are broad and thin.

109
00:05:18,710 --> 00:05:21,140
Broad means a large surface area,

110
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:23,050
to absorb more light.

111
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:27,770
Thin means a short distance for carbon
dioxide to diffuse to the cells

112
00:05:27,770 --> 00:05:28,810
inside.

113
00:05:29,310 --> 00:05:31,600
Now let's cut a leaf open.

114
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:36,390
This is a cross-section through
the leaf of a dicotyledonous plant.

115
00:05:36,390 --> 00:05:40,050
That's a plant whose seeds
have two seed leaves.

116
00:05:40,050 --> 00:05:42,460
It's a simplified diagram.

117
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:45,150
Everyone needs to name each part.

118
00:05:45,150 --> 00:05:50,240
Explaining how each part helps
photosynthesis is for the Extended paper.

119
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:54,330
Let's go through it layer
by layer, from the top.

120
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:57,080
First, the waxy cuticle.

121
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:58,780
It reduces water loss,

122
00:05:58,780 --> 00:06:00,780
and because it's transparent,

123
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:03,680
light passes straight through it.

124
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:06,030
Next, the upper epidermis.

125
00:06:06,030 --> 00:06:08,320
These cells are transparent too,

126
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:10,510
and they have no chloroplasts,

127
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:14,180
so light passes through
to the cells below.

128
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:16,440
Then the palisade mesophyll.

129
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:18,090
These cells are tall,

130
00:06:18,090 --> 00:06:21,200
tightly packed, close
to the top surface,

131
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:23,310
and full of chloroplasts.

132
00:06:23,310 --> 00:06:25,850
So they absorb the most light.

133
00:06:25,850 --> 00:06:29,090
This is where most
photosynthesis happens.

134
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:33,320
Below the palisade is
the spongy mesophyll.

135
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:35,020
Its cells are rounder,

136
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:36,480
and loosely packed,

137
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:38,880
with air spaces between them.

138
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:42,770
The air spaces let carbon
dioxide diffuse to the cells,

139
00:06:42,770 --> 00:06:46,870
and they give a large surface
area for gas exchange.

140
00:06:47,370 --> 00:06:50,800
Running through the leaf
are vascular bundles.

141
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:54,900
The xylem brings water and
mineral ions into the leaf.

142
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:58,260
The phloem carries sucrose
and amino acids away,

143
00:06:58,260 --> 00:07:00,650
to the rest of the plant.

144
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:04,020
On the underside is
the lower epidermis,

145
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:06,520
with tiny pores called stomata.

146
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,910
One pore is called a stoma.

147
00:07:08,910 --> 00:07:12,130
Carbon dioxide diffuses
in through the stomata,

148
00:07:12,130 --> 00:07:14,190
and oxygen diffuses out.

149
00:07:14,190 --> 00:07:18,620
Each stoma is opened and closed
by a pair of guard cells.

150
00:07:18,620 --> 00:07:21,480
In the light, they open the stomata,

151
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:24,270
so carbon dioxide can diffuse in.

152
00:07:24,770 --> 00:07:26,880
So, from top to bottom:

153
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,830
cuticle, upper epidermis,

154
00:07:28,830 --> 00:07:30,200
palisade mesophyll,

155
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:32,690
spongy mesophyll, vascular bundle,

156
00:07:32,690 --> 00:07:36,170
lower epidermis with
stomata and guard cells.

157
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:41,760
So how can you show that a leaf
has been photosynthesising?

158
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:43,310
Test it for starch,

159
00:07:43,310 --> 00:07:47,410
because a leaf stores some
of its glucose as starch.

160
00:07:47,910 --> 00:07:50,260
First, destarch the plant.

161
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:53,460
Put it in the dark for a day or two.

162
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:56,380
With no light, it
can't photosynthesise,

163
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:59,110
so it uses up its stored starch.

164
00:07:59,110 --> 00:08:03,730
That means any starch you find later
must have been made during your

165
00:08:03,730 --> 00:08:06,420
experiment. Step one:

166
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:10,270
put the leaf in boiling
water for about a minute.

167
00:08:10,270 --> 00:08:11,920
This kills the cells,

168
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:14,450
and breaks down the cell membranes,

169
00:08:14,450 --> 00:08:18,480
so the iodine can get
in later. Step two:

170
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,780
turn off the Bunsen burner.

171
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:24,270
Then put the leaf in a
boiling tube of ethanol,

172
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:26,900
and stand it in the hot water.

173
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:28,460
Ethanol is flammable,

174
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:31,480
so never heat it with a naked flame.

175
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:34,260
The hot ethanol removes
the chlorophyll,

176
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:39,070
so the colour change will
be easy to see. Step three:

177
00:08:39,070 --> 00:08:41,460
dip the leaf in warm water.

178
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:43,600
The ethanol makes it brittle,

179
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:47,200
and the water softens it. Step four:

180
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:49,670
spread the leaf on a white tile,

181
00:08:49,670 --> 00:08:51,990
so the colour is easy to see,

182
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:54,150
and add iodine solution.

183
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:56,150
If it turns blue-black,

184
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:57,820
starch is present.

185
00:08:57,820 --> 00:08:59,620
If it stays orange-brown,

186
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:01,340
there's no starch.

187
00:09:02,490 --> 00:09:06,980
Now you can use that test to
show what photosynthesis needs.

188
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:09,530
Each experiment needs a control.

189
00:09:09,530 --> 00:09:12,150
A control is identical to the test,

190
00:09:12,150 --> 00:09:15,580
except for the one factor
you're investigating.

191
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:19,630
It shows that the result
was caused by that factor.

192
00:09:20,130 --> 00:09:21,950
First, chlorophyll.

193
00:09:21,950 --> 00:09:25,250
Take a destarched plant
with variegated leaves:

194
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:28,770
leaves that are partly
green and partly white.

195
00:09:28,770 --> 00:09:31,610
The white parts have no chlorophyll.

196
00:09:31,610 --> 00:09:34,560
Leave it in the light
for a few hours,

197
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:36,270
then test a leaf.

198
00:09:36,270 --> 00:09:39,110
Only the green parts turn blue-black.

199
00:09:39,110 --> 00:09:41,710
The white parts stay orange-brown.

200
00:09:41,710 --> 00:09:44,350
The green parts are the control.

201
00:09:44,350 --> 00:09:46,560
So chlorophyll is needed.

202
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:48,630
Second, light.

203
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:50,430
Take a destarched plant,

204
00:09:50,430 --> 00:09:53,940
and cover part of one
leaf with black paper.

205
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:57,150
Leave it in the light
for a few hours.

206
00:09:57,150 --> 00:10:01,450
After the test, only the
uncovered part turns blue-black.

207
00:10:01,450 --> 00:10:04,190
The uncovered part is the control.

208
00:10:04,190 --> 00:10:06,100
So light is needed.

209
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,660
Third, carbon dioxide.

210
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:10,460
Take a destarched plant,

211
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:11,960
and seal one leaf,

212
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:15,410
still attached, inside
a flask with soda lime,

213
00:10:15,410 --> 00:10:17,720
which absorbs carbon dioxide.

214
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:20,200
The control is an identical flask,

215
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,960
with no soda lime.

216
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:24,380
After a few hours in the light,

217
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:27,320
only the control leaf
turns blue-black.

218
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:29,770
So carbon dioxide is needed.

219
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:34,380
Next: how fast is
photosynthesis happening?

220
00:10:34,380 --> 00:10:35,900
That's its rate.

221
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:39,650
To measure it, use
pondweed, a water plant.

222
00:10:39,650 --> 00:10:43,450
Put it in water with a little
sodium hydrogencarbonate,

223
00:10:43,450 --> 00:10:45,810
which supplies carbon dioxide.

224
00:10:45,810 --> 00:10:51,220
In the light, the pondweed gives
off bubbles of gas, mostly oxygen.

225
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,920
Count the bubbles per minute.

226
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:56,300
Or, for more accurate results,

227
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:59,120
collect the gas and
measure its volume,

228
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:02,210
because bubbles can
be different sizes.

229
00:11:02,710 --> 00:11:04,900
To change the light intensity,

230
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:07,780
move a lamp closer or further away.

231
00:11:07,780 --> 00:11:09,380
The closer the lamp,

232
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:11,880
the higher the light intensity.

233
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:15,420
So, light intensity is
the independent variable:

234
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:17,230
the one you change.

235
00:11:17,230 --> 00:11:19,840
The rate is the dependent variable:

236
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,700
the one you measure.

237
00:11:21,700 --> 00:11:24,750
And everything else
must be kept constant:

238
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:28,600
the same plant, the same
carbon dioxide concentration,

239
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,160
the same temperature,

240
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:32,260
and no other lights on.

241
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:34,500
To keep the temperature steady,

242
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:37,280
stand the beaker in a water bath.

243
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,780
An LED lamp helps,

244
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:43,220
because it gives off much less
heat than a filament bulb.

245
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:45,170
At each new distance,

246
00:11:45,170 --> 00:11:47,840
wait a few minutes before you count,

247
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:49,990
so the plant can adjust.

248
00:11:49,990 --> 00:11:53,020
Then repeat, and calculate a mean.

249
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:57,320
You can test the other
two factors the same way.

250
00:11:57,320 --> 00:12:00,050
Just change one thing at a time.

251
00:12:00,050 --> 00:12:01,800
To vary carbon dioxide,

252
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:05,690
use different concentrations
of sodium hydrogencarbonate.

253
00:12:05,690 --> 00:12:07,200
To vary temperature,

254
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:10,680
set the water bath to
different temperatures.

255
00:12:11,830 --> 00:12:13,740
Here are the results.

256
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:15,790
As light intensity increases,

257
00:12:15,790 --> 00:12:18,590
the rate of photosynthesis increases.

258
00:12:18,590 --> 00:12:20,500
Then it levels off.

259
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:23,590
Increase the carbon
dioxide concentration,

260
00:12:23,590 --> 00:12:25,800
and you get the same shape:

261
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:27,260
the rate increases,

262
00:12:27,260 --> 00:12:28,930
then levels off.

263
00:12:29,230 --> 00:12:31,250
Temperature is different.

264
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:33,920
The rate increases up to an optimum,

265
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:35,640
then falls quickly.

266
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:40,590
That's because the reactions of
photosynthesis are catalysed by enzymes.

267
00:12:40,590 --> 00:12:43,860
This next part is for
the Extended paper.

268
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:45,270
Below the optimum,

269
00:12:45,270 --> 00:12:49,520
raising the temperature gives the
molecules more kinetic energy,

270
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:54,210
so there are more frequent effective
collisions between enzymes and their

271
00:12:54,210 --> 00:12:56,760
substrates. Above the optimum,

272
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:58,920
the enzymes are denatured.

273
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:01,210
Their active sites change shape,

274
00:13:01,210 --> 00:13:03,950
so the substrates no longer fit.

275
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:07,220
When a question says
describe a graph,

276
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:10,960
say what happens, and quote
numbers from the axes,

277
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,580
with their units.

278
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:15,410
When it says explain, say why.

279
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:18,310
For the Extended paper,

280
00:13:18,310 --> 00:13:22,720
you need to explain those
shapes using limiting factors.

281
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:27,630
A limiting factor is something in
short supply that limits the rate of a

282
00:13:27,630 --> 00:13:28,720
process.

283
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:31,370
Back to the light graph.

284
00:13:31,370 --> 00:13:32,970
On this rising part,

285
00:13:32,970 --> 00:13:36,500
the rate increases as
light intensity increases.

286
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:39,730
So light intensity is
the limiting factor.

287
00:13:39,730 --> 00:13:41,230
On this flat part,

288
00:13:41,230 --> 00:13:43,730
more light makes no difference.

289
00:13:43,730 --> 00:13:47,400
Light intensity is no
longer the limiting factor.

290
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:48,810
Something else is,

291
00:13:48,810 --> 00:13:52,640
like carbon dioxide
concentration, or temperature.

292
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:57,890
Now repeat the experiment at a
higher carbon dioxide concentration.

293
00:13:57,890 --> 00:13:59,640
At low light intensity,

294
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:01,820
the two curves are the same,

295
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:05,690
because light intensity is
still the limiting factor.

296
00:14:05,690 --> 00:14:08,750
But the new curve keeps
rising for longer,

297
00:14:08,750 --> 00:14:10,710
and levels off higher.

298
00:14:10,710 --> 00:14:15,740
That shows carbon dioxide was the
limiting factor on the flat part.

299
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:19,200
In the exam, name
the limiting factor,

300
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,880
and give the reason:

301
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:23,580
increasing it increases the rate.

302
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:27,770
Different conditions have
different limiting factors.

303
00:14:27,770 --> 00:14:30,130
At dawn, or on a dull day,

304
00:14:30,130 --> 00:14:33,350
light intensity is usually
the limiting factor,

305
00:14:33,350 --> 00:14:35,800
because there's not much light.

306
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:37,590
On a cold winter's day,

307
00:14:37,590 --> 00:14:39,460
it's often temperature.

308
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:42,190
The molecules have
less kinetic energy,

309
00:14:42,190 --> 00:14:45,230
so there are fewer
effective collisions.

310
00:14:45,230 --> 00:14:47,990
And on a bright, warm summer's day,

311
00:14:47,990 --> 00:14:50,470
there's plenty of light and warmth,

312
00:14:50,470 --> 00:14:53,610
so it's often carbon
dioxide concentration.

313
00:14:53,610 --> 00:14:57,950
There's only a tiny amount of
carbon dioxide in the air.

314
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:00,560
One more practical,

315
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:03,840
and this one's for
the Extended paper.

316
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:08,040
Hydrogencarbonate indicator shows
how much carbon dioxide is in a

317
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:13,460
solution. At the normal level of
carbon dioxide in air, it's red.

318
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:15,310
With more carbon dioxide,

319
00:15:15,310 --> 00:15:16,880
it turns yellow.

320
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:18,730
With less carbon dioxide,

321
00:15:18,730 --> 00:15:20,400
it turns purple.

322
00:15:20,900 --> 00:15:23,640
Here are three tubes of indicator.

323
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:25,490
They're sealed with bungs,

324
00:15:25,490 --> 00:15:29,670
so no carbon dioxide from
the air can get in or out.

325
00:15:29,670 --> 00:15:32,600
One has pondweed, in bright light.

326
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:34,250
One has pondweed too,

327
00:15:34,250 --> 00:15:36,720
but its tube is wrapped in foil,

328
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:38,530
so it's dark inside.

329
00:15:38,530 --> 00:15:41,510
And one has no pondweed at all.

330
00:15:41,510 --> 00:15:43,790
What colour will each tube be,

331
00:15:43,790 --> 00:15:45,650
after a few hours?

332
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:49,670
Pause the video, and
make your prediction.

333
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:56,040
Here's what happens.

334
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:59,410
In the light, the
indicator turns purple.

335
00:15:59,410 --> 00:16:02,200
Photosynthesis is faster
than respiration,

336
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:07,030
so the pondweed takes in more
carbon dioxide than it gives out.

337
00:16:07,330 --> 00:16:10,010
In the dark, it turns yellow.

338
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:11,770
There's no photosynthesis,

339
00:16:11,770 --> 00:16:13,720
but respiration carries on,

340
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:17,000
so the pondweed gives
out carbon dioxide.

341
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:20,230
The tube with no pondweed stays red.

342
00:16:20,230 --> 00:16:21,900
That's the control.

343
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:25,960
It shows that the pondweed
caused the colour changes.

344
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:30,100
And in dim light, the
two rates can be equal.

345
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:33,990
Then there's no net uptake or
release of carbon dioxide,

346
00:16:33,990 --> 00:16:36,390
so the indicator stays red.

347
00:16:36,890 --> 00:16:39,010
Which busts a classic myth:

348
00:16:39,010 --> 00:16:41,750
that plants only respire at night.

349
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:43,840
Plants respire all the time,

350
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:46,520
day and night, just like you.

351
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:49,930
In bright light,
photosynthesis is just faster,

352
00:16:49,930 --> 00:16:53,200
so there's a net uptake
of carbon dioxide.

353
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:54,690
Net means overall:

354
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:59,030
the plant takes in more carbon
dioxide than it gives out.

355
00:16:59,030 --> 00:17:02,010
Net is the word examiners look for.

356
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:05,990
So, back to van Helmont's willow.

357
00:17:05,990 --> 00:17:09,620
Where did those seventy-four
kilograms come from?

358
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:12,350
Carbon dioxide, from the air,

359
00:17:12,350 --> 00:17:14,740
and water, from the soil.

360
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:16,250
Joined into glucose,

361
00:17:16,250 --> 00:17:18,050
using energy from light,

362
00:17:18,050 --> 00:17:19,950
then built into cellulose,

363
00:17:19,950 --> 00:17:21,820
starch and proteins.

364
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:25,960
The little that the soil lost
was mostly mineral ions,

365
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:28,270
like nitrate and magnesium.

366
00:17:28,670 --> 00:17:32,330
Van Helmont thought his
tree was made of water.

367
00:17:32,330 --> 00:17:34,530
He was only partly right.

368
00:17:34,530 --> 00:17:37,210
A living tree is full of water.

369
00:17:37,210 --> 00:17:41,340
But most of the wood itself
was built from carbon dioxide,

370
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:43,490
taken out of thin air.

371
00:17:44,640 --> 00:17:46,170
Let's recap.

372
00:17:46,170 --> 00:17:50,890
Photosynthesis: carbon dioxide plus
water gives glucose plus oxygen,

373
00:17:50,890 --> 00:17:54,070
in the presence of
light and chlorophyll.

374
00:17:54,070 --> 00:17:58,630
Chlorophyll transfers energy from
light into energy in chemicals.

375
00:17:58,630 --> 00:18:00,920
Glucose is used for respiration,

376
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:02,430
starch, cellulose,

377
00:18:02,430 --> 00:18:04,150
sucrose and nectar.

378
00:18:04,150 --> 00:18:07,570
Nitrate ions are needed
to make amino acids.

379
00:18:07,570 --> 00:18:11,000
Magnesium ions are needed
to make chlorophyll.

380
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,940
Leaves are broad, thin,

381
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:14,540
and built in layers,

382
00:18:14,540 --> 00:18:17,000
each adapted for photosynthesis.

383
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:21,740
Light intensity, carbon dioxide
concentration and temperature can all be

384
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:23,370
limiting factors.

385
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:26,130
And that's plant nutrition.
